+These bits are encoded so that most of the time they will take the same value as the *updiscon* field, and will therefore compress away, having no impact on the encoding efficiency.  If implicit_return mode is enabled, the encoder keeps track of function calls and returns, and does not generate _te_inst_ packets for return target addresses that can be inferred by the decoder, as described in section <<sec:implicit-return>>.
